# relay — configuration. Every value is overridable from the environment, and
# anything you put in `config.local` (git-ignored) wins over this file.

# ---- when to hand over -----------------------------------------------------

# Handover fires at this % of the context window. 85 rather than 90 on purpose:
# the final tail digest has to finish BEFORE auto-compact (the backstop) kicks
# in, and that costs a few seconds.
RELAY_PCT=${RELAY_PCT:-85}

# Assumed context window in tokens. Self-correcting: a 200k session can never
# report more than ~200k, so the first sighting of >190k rewrites this to 1M for
# that project. Set it explicitly if you already know.
RELAY_WINDOW=${RELAY_WINDOW:-200000}

# ---- cost control ----------------------------------------------------------

# Map-step model. Cheap on purpose: this is line reduction, not thinking.
RELAY_MODEL=${RELAY_MODEL:-claude-haiku-4-5-20251001}

# The claude binary. Hooks inherit the session's PATH, which is not always the
# one you get over ssh/cron — set an absolute path here if `claude` is not found.
RELAY_CLAUDE=${RELAY_CLAUDE:-claude}

# Don't call the model every turn — let the transcript tail reach this many
# bytes first. Lower = fresher brief, higher = cheaper.
RELAY_MIN_BYTES=${RELAY_MIN_BYTES:-20000}

# The brief gets folded (re-compressed by the model) once it passes this size.
RELAY_BRIEF_CAP=${RELAY_BRIEF_CAP:-60000}

# ---- what gets injected at handover ----------------------------------------

# Total chars of brief + verbatim tail handed to the cleared session.
RELAY_SEED_CAP=${RELAY_SEED_CAP:-35000}

# Transcript lines kept VERBATIM. Compressed history is lossy exactly where it
# hurts most — the thing you were in the middle of — so the recent tail is
# passed through raw.
RELAY_TAIL_LINES=${RELAY_TAIL_LINES:-160}

# ---- notification ----------------------------------------------------------

# ntfy.sh topic for the "session is full, hit /clear" push. Empty = no push.
# Put this in config.local, not here — a topic name is a shared secret.
RELAY_NTFY=${RELAY_NTFY:-}

# ---- prompts (change these to work in your own language) -------------------

RELAY_DIGEST_PROMPT=${RELAY_DIGEST_PROMPT:-"This is an excerpt from a Claude Code transcript (U: user, A: assistant, TOOL/RES: tool calls and their results).
Write a compact log of what ACTUALLY happened, as a bullet list, max 15 bullets:
- decisions taken, and why
- files changed (full path) and what the change did
- commands/tools run and WHAT RESULT they produced
- open threads, TODOs, and what the user is waiting for
- gotchas, and things that turned out not to work
Distinguish what was claimed from what was demonstrated. No preamble, no closing
remarks, no headings. Bullets only."}

RELAY_FOLD_PROMPT=${RELAY_FOLD_PROMPT:-"This is a log of a long working session. Compress it to roughly half its
length without losing: decisions taken, file paths, commands and their results,
open threads. Merge repetition. Keep chronological order. Bullets only, no prose."}

# NOTE: keep the literal string RELAY-BRIEF-V1 in this header. It is the
# sentinel that stops the digester from summarising its own summaries.
RELAY_SEED_HEADER=${RELAY_SEED_HEADER:-"RELAY-BRIEF-V1 — automatic handover. The previous session filled its context
window and was cleared; what follows IS your memory of it. Continue the work,
do not start over, and do not ask the user what happened."}

RELAY_SEED_PAST=${RELAY_SEED_PAST:-"## What has been done (compressed log)"}
RELAY_SEED_TAIL=${RELAY_SEED_TAIL:-"## Most recent turns, verbatim (U=user, A=you, TOOL/RES=tools)"}
